    "title": "Nancy Mace criticizes Senate Democrats and highlights military pay concerns on X - Berkeley Leader",
    "text": "U.S. Representative Nancy Mace, who serves South Carolina’s 1st district, posted a series of statements on her official X account on October 15, 2025. The posts included commentary on recent political developments and the ongoing government funding situation.\nIn a post at 19:33 UTC, Mace wrote: “Roses are red. Violets are blue. Funny how justice Came looking for you.”\nLater that evening, at 20:29 UTC, she criticized Senate Democrats with the statement: “‘America Last’ brought to you by Senate Democrats.”\nAt 20:58 UTC, Mace addressed the issue of military pay during a government shutdown, stating: ” Thanks to President Trump, $8B in unused defense funds are being used to cover mid-month paychecks. But this is a one-time fix. If Democrats don’t reopen the government by the end of the month, our troops will miss their next paycheck.”\nNancy Mace has represented South Carolina’s 1st District in Congress since 2021 and previously served in the South Carolina House of Representatives from 2018 to 2020. She succeeded Joe Cunningham as representative for the district. Born in Fort Bragg, North Carolina in 1977, Mace resides in Charleston and graduated from The Citadel with a Bachelor of Science degree in 1999.",
